    lvxSub_playlist: "Your songs, one after the other, for a whole set.",
    lvxHelp_transport: "PLAY / STOP: as the PLAY button. REC: records into the track you play (as REC on the FM-1); in an empty project, REC again closes the loop. undo / redo: the last recording or edit.\nBPM: drag the knob up or down (Shift: fine), or tap TAP in time. SWING: from straight to shuffled. The counter shows bar.beat, and in song mode the part and bar of the song.\nloop / song: the loop playing, or the song (the sections in order). song rec: the order you play the sections becomes the song. FILL while held, FILL BAR: the next bar is a fill (the steps marked “fill only” play).\nall off: lets go of every note and effect. full screen: the page alone.\nThe second row: the clock and the set's time (tap it to start again), record set (a WAV of what the FM-1 plays, from its USB audio), MIDI learn and lock (see their tips).",
    lvxHelp_sections: "A section is a whole loop: every track's patterns, sounds and mix. A song is A, B, C, D — for example A intro, B verse, C chorus, D break.\nTo make one: play the loop you want, then under “save the loop into” press a letter. A used section asks before it is replaced.\nTo switch: tap A–D (or keys 1–4). Playing, the new section starts at the next bar (it blinks while it waits); stopped, at once.\nSections change WHAT plays (the notes). To change HOW it sounds without changing the notes, use the scenes.\nchain: tap two or more letters (A B B C…), then play chain: each section plays for its own bars, then the next, and the chain loops — as SAVE + several keys on the FM-1. stop chain goes back to one section.",
    lvxHelp_scenes: "A scene is a photo of your knobs: each track's level, mute, pan, filter, sends, drive, sound knobs, envelope, LFO, INSERT and arp, and the master effects. It does not touch the notes.\nExample: scene 1 “intro” = filters closed, drums low, little reverb; scene 2 “drop” = everything open and loud. Play your loop, tap 1, then 2 at the drop: the FM-1 jumps from one sound to the other.\nTo store: set the knobs as you want them, press STORE, then a scene pad. Double-click a pad to name it. F1–F8 recall, Shift+F1–F8 store.\nmorph: “at once” jumps; 1–16 bars glides there slowly (a build-up). + sounds: the scene also loads its presets and kit. + tempo: it also sets the BPM.\nThe crossfader: pick two scenes (A and B) and slide between them by hand, like a DJ.",
    lvxHelp_mixer: "One strip per track (1–3 synths, D drums). The list and ‹ › change the sound (the drums: the kit); ☆ makes it a favourite.\nThe fader is the level (its meter beside it); the thin bar under the sound is where the pattern is.\nfilt: left a low-pass (darker), right a high-pass (thinner). pan: left / right. rev, dly, cho: how much goes to the reverb, delay, chorus. drive: saturation.\nmute / solo: as GLO + key. play: the keys below and the PERFORM card follow this track (it is selected on the FM-1 too, so REC records it).",
    lvxHelp_keys: "The keys play the track chosen with “play” (or the track buttons here), as real MIDI notes: they sound at once, and REC records them.\nOn the computer: A W S E D F T G Y H U J K O L P are the keys (white and black), Z / X change the octave. For the drums, the same letters are the 16 pads, with four strengths (GHOST, SOFT, NORM, HARD).\nvelocity: how hard the keys play. arp: the track's arpeggiator mode, hold: notes keep playing after you let go.\nplay / roll / erase: what the keys and pads do. roll repeats the note or drum sound while you hold it, at the roll rate (as ARP + key); playing with REC on, it is recorded. erase removes that note or drum sound from the pattern while you hold it: playing, the steps it passes; stopped, every step (as EDIT + key; undo brings it back).",
    lvxHelp_perform: "Everything you can turn on the track you play, without menus.\nsound: the engine's own values (as the FM-1's EDIT page), the three macros (FLT PIT SHP), the envelope and glide, the LFO.\narp & key: the arpeggiator (mode, rate, octaves, gate, swing, order, hold); the key (root, scale, chord, transpose) — “every synth track” sends the key to all three synths.\ninsert & bus: the track's INSERT effect and filter; the shared delay, reverb, chorus, TEXTURE (a background bed) and the metronome.\nsteps: the pattern as a grid. Tap a step to turn it on or off (a new synth step plays the last note you played); right-click for its fill condition (yellow: only in a fill, red: never in a fill). LEN, DIV, SWG, GATE: the pattern's length, speed, swing and note length.\nThe drums' sound tab: pick a pad, then its tune (semitones) and decay, as the DRUMS screen's SOUND page. The steps tab's pattern buttons: shift the whole pattern a step, half or double its length, transpose it — each one undo.",
    lvxHelp_fx: "Punch-in effects play only while you hold the pad (or Shift + a letter key), then the sound comes back exactly as it was: nothing is recorded or changed.\nloops & time: repeat the last beats (LOOP 4 … 32), stutter, reverse, stop, half speed, rewind, freeze. filter & EQ: low / high pass, kill a band, phone. colour: crush, alias, octave up, flanger, echo. movement: gate, wobble, auto-pan, mono, fade out.\nlatch: a tap turns the effect on and it stays; another tap (or another effect) turns it off.",
    lvxHelp_master: "These act on the whole mix, after the tracks.\nfilter: a DJ filter (left darker, right thinner, middle off). dust: lo-fi — noise, wobble and grit. duck: the kick pushes the other tracks down (the “pumping” of dance music).\nvolume: the FM-1's level from here; turning its MASTER knob takes it back (knob: at once). rev throw / echo throw: hold for every track to pour into the reverb or the delay, as FX + OCT- / OCT+ — let go and it falls back.",
    lvxHelp_playlist: "For a set of several songs. First, save each song as a file: Save & load → Export this song (the loop, A–D and their order).\nadd songs: put the files here. Tap a song (or next song, key N): the FM-1 stops, loads it in a few seconds and, with “play when loaded”, starts.\n✎ gives a song its tempo (set when it loads) and a cue — a note for you on stage, shown while it plays, with the next song under it.\nsave the list: one file with the songs, your scenes and your MIDI mappings, to take to the gig. The list also stays in this browser.",
